 "streaming": "Every border is a swinging door (the eskinita's mouth is a bend), and every way through goes both ways: no drops. Whichever way you walk, crossing into a section loads the next one beyond it and unloads the one furthest behind. A border door stays shut until the section behind it is loaded, and unloading waits until you're a few metres past a door, so stepping back and forth through it doesn't reload anything. A section remembers what's done (fights, pickups, inspects) when it unloads, so walking back never brings the dead back.",
